The latest MSTest is **4.2.3**. Upgrading from 3.8.0 to v4 has several breaking changes. Here's what affects **your project specifically**:

---

## 1. `[ExpectedException]` is removed (critical for your code)

Your two tests use `[ExpectedException(...)]` which no longer exists in v4. Replace with `Assert.ThrowsExactly<T>()`:

```csharp
// Before
[ExpectedException(typeof(ArgumentNullException))]
[TestMethod]
public void Validate_NullInput_ThrowsArgumentNull()
{
    Validate(null);
}

// After
[TestMethod]
public void Validate_NullInput_ThrowsArgumentNull()
{
    Assert.ThrowsExactly<ArgumentNullException>(() => Validate(null));
}
```

## 2. Analyzer MSTEST0032 becomes a **warning**

Your `Assert.IsTrue(true)` will trigger warning MSTEST0032 (always-true assertion). Replace it with a meaningful assertion or remove it.

## 3. Other v4 breaking changes (less likely to affect you)

| Change | Impact |
|--------|--------|
| `TestMethodAttribute.Execute` → `ExecuteAsync` | Only if you have custom test method attributes |
| `ClassCleanupBehavior` enum removed | Only if you use `ClassCleanup(ClassCleanupBehavior.EndOfClass)` |
| `TestContext.Properties` is now `IDictionary<string, object>` | Only if you access properties |
| `Assert` APIs no longer accept `message` + `params object[]` | Use string interpolation instead |
| Dropped .NET < 8 support | You're on net8.0, so you're fine |

---

## To upgrade

Update your `.csproj`:
```xml
<PackageReference Include="MSTest" Version="4.2.3" />
```

And fix your tests like:
```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void Validate_NullInput_ThrowsArgumentNull()
{
    Assert.ThrowsExactly<ArgumentNullException>(() => Validate(null));
}

[TestMethod]
public void Process_InvalidState_ThrowsInvalidOperation()
{
    Assert.ThrowsExactly<InvalidOperationException>(() => Process());
}
```

Full migration guide: https://learn.microsoft.com/dotnet/core/testing/unit-testing-mstest-migration-v3-v4

Would you like me to apply these changes to your project?
